IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-11: Article 11 (technical documentation) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744.
-- The Omnibus replaced the second subparagraph of paragraph 1: the simplified manner of providing the Annex IV elements, first for SMEs, including start-ups, and a simplified form for small and microenterprises, now also for SMCs,
-- with the duty of an SME or SMC that opts for it to use the form, and the duty of notified bodies to accept the form. The sentences of that subparagraph that did not change in substance (the demonstrate-and-inform sentence and the Annex IV sentence) are one function each;
-- the three that changed are each encoded in both versions (each text in its own function with no date and no gate, a dispatcher gated by Article 113 with Article 111(2) that reads the version in force). The branch that reads the text as enacted is dead:
-- Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 applied as enacted from 2 August 2026, after the Omnibus took effect (27 July 2026). The old text is tested through its own function.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met (or the liberty is open); JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered. The duties of the Commission (the form, the delegated acts) take no AI system and no date gate: fork F-commission-no-gate.

§ `Article 11(1): the technical documentation`

-- src:312 | 1. The technical documentation of a high-risk AI system shall be drawn up before that system is placed on the market or put into service and shall be kept up-to date.
@ref Art 11(1) first subparagraph (src:312)
-- A flat "shall" in the passive: no party is named, so no regulative rule (fork F-party-less; listed under Rules with no breach path). "before that system is placed on the market or put into service": the drawing-up date must fall before the core record's placed date.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the date on which the technical documentation of the high-risk AI system was drawn up` IS A DATE
      `the technical documentation is kept up-to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) first subparagraph the technical documentation is drawn up before the placing on the market and kept up to date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST ((`the date on which the technical documentation of the high-risk AI system was drawn up` LESS THAN (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`)) AND `the technical documentation is kept up-to date`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be drawn up before that system is placed on the market or put into service and shall be kept up-to date"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:314 | That technical documentation shall be drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate that the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in this Section and to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information in a clear and comprehensive form to assess the compliance of the AI system with those requirements.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | The technical documentation shall be drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate that the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in this Section and to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information in a clear and comprehensive form to assess the compliance of the AI system with those requirements.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph first sentence (src:314) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
-- VERSIONS: the sentence is the same in both texts but for "The" (as enacted) and "That" (as amended): one function, both quoted.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation is drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate that the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in this Section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation is drawn up in such a way as to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information in a clear and comprehensive form to assess the compliance of the AI system with those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) second subparagraph first sentence the technical documentation is drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate compliance and to inform` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation is drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate that the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in this Section` AND `the technical documentation is drawn up in such a way as to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information in a clear and comprehensive form to assess the compliance of the AI system with those requirements`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That technical documentation shall be drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate ... and to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:314 | It shall contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | It shall contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph second sentence (src:314) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
-- The elements of Annex IV are answered by `Annex IV the technical documentation contains the elements ...` in P2-annex-iv.l4; this function takes that answer as a yes or no (seam: Annex IV).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) second subparagraph second sentence the technical documentation contains at a minimum the elements set out in Annex IV` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It shall contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 11(1), second subparagraph: the simplified manner, the form, the SME and SMC liberty`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | SMEs, including start-ups, may provide the elements of the technical documentation specified in Annex IV in a simplified manner.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, SME liberty, as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
-- VERSION as enacted. A liberty ("may provide"): JUST TRUE for an SME; NOTHING for any other provider (the text is silent on them).
GIVEN `the provider is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) as enacted the provider may provide the elements of the technical documentation in a simplified manner` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the provider is an SME, including a start-up`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "SMEs, including start-ups, may provide": the liberty is the SME's (a grant limited by its own wording)
    ELSE JUST (TRUE)

-- src:314 | SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, may provide the elements of the technical documentation specified in Annex IV in a simplified manner.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, SME liberty, as amended (src:314)
-- VERSION as amended: SMCs added.
GIVEN `the provider is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) as amended the provider may provide the elements of the technical documentation in a simplified manner` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the provider is an SME, including a start-up` OR `the provider is an SMC`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, may provide": the liberty is the SME's or the SMC's (a grant limited by its own wording)
    ELSE JUST (TRUE)

-- src:314 | SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, may provide the elements of the technical documentation specified in Annex IV in a simplified manner.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | SMEs, including start-ups, may provide the elements of the technical documentation specified in Annex IV in a simplified manner.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, SME liberty (src:314) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the provider is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) the provider may provide the elements of the technical documentation in a simplified manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 11(1) as enacted the provider may provide the elements of the technical documentation in a simplified manner` `the provider is an SME, including a start-up`  -- VERSION as enacted
        WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 11(1) as amended the provider may provide the elements of the technical documentation in a simplified manner` `the provider is an SME, including a start-up` `the provider is an SMC`  -- VERSION as amended
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | To that end, the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, the form, as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
-- VERSION as enacted. The Commission's duty; no date and no AI system (fork F-commission-no-gate). The Commission has no seat: the function is the answer to a question about it.
GIVEN `the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) as enacted the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises` MEANS
    JUST (`the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises"

-- src:314 | To that end, the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, the form, as amended (src:314)
-- VERSION as amended: the form is targeted at SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs.
GIVEN `the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) as amended the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs and SMCs` MEANS
    JUST (`the Commission has established a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs"

-- src:314 | Where an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner, it shall use the form referred to in this paragraph.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, use of the form (src:314)
-- VERSION as amended only: the as-enacted text has no such sentence, so the as-enacted branch answers NOTHING (silent); no date the gate admits reaches it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, and opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has used the form referred to in this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) the provider that opts for the simplified manner has used the simplified technical documentation form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the Omnibus inserted this sentence; the text as enacted has none (a branch no date reaches: fork F-10-5-dead)
        WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
            IF NOT (`the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, and opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner": a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-duty-where
            ELSE JUST (`the provider has used the form referred to in this paragraph`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall use the form referred to in this paragraph"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:314 | Notified bodies shall accept the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, notified bodies accept the form (src:314)
-- VERSION as amended only: the as-enacted text has no such sentence, so the as-enacted branch answers NOTHING (silent); no date the gate admits reaches it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the documentation is provided on the form referred to in this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has accepted the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) the notified body has accepted the simplified technical documentation form for the purposes of the conformity assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the Omnibus inserted this sentence; the text as enacted has none (a branch no date reaches: fork F-10-5-dead)
        WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
            IF NOT (`the documentation is provided on the form referred to in this paragraph`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notified bodies shall accept the form": the sentence is silent on documentation that is not provided on that form (no "where" of its own), fork F-duty-where
            ELSE JUST (`the notified body has accepted the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall accept the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 11(2): a single set of technical documentation`

-- src:316 | 2. Where a high-risk AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I is placed on the market or put into service, a single set of technical documentation shall be drawn up containing all the information set out in paragraph 1, as well as the information required under those legal acts.
@ref Art 11(2) (src:316)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I and is placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a single set of technical documentation has been drawn up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the single set contains all the information set out in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the single set contains the information required under those legal acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(2) a single set of technical documentation has been drawn up containing all the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I and is placed on the market or put into service`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a high-risk AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I is placed on the market or put into service": a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-duty-where
        ELSE JUST (`a single set of technical documentation has been drawn up` AND `the single set contains all the information set out in paragraph 1` AND `the single set contains the information required under those legal acts`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a single set of technical documentation shall be drawn up containing all the information set out in paragraph 1, as well as the information required under those legal acts"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 11(3): delegated acts amending Annex IV`

-- src:317 | 3. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annex IV, where necessary, to ensure that, in light of technical progress, the technical documentation provides all the information necessary to assess the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in this Section.
@ref Art 11(3) (src:317)
-- A power of the Commission (the person's liability: the technical documentation they must produce may change); no AI system and no date gate (fork F-commission-no-gate). No seat: an official.
-- The gate "where necessary" is a "where" condition on a power: when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE (the Guide's periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); the other reading is NOTHING (the grant line); fork F-11-3-necessary (split site ii).
GIVEN `amending Annex IV is necessary to ensure that, in light of technical progress, the technical documentation provides all the information necessary to assess the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in this Section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegated act is adopted in accordance with Article 97` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(3) the Commission may adopt delegated acts to amend Annex IV` MEANS
    JUST (`amending Annex IV is necessary to ensure that, in light of technical progress, the technical documentation provides all the information necessary to assess the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in this Section` AND `the delegated act is adopted in accordance with Article 97`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annex IV, where necessary, to ensure that, in light of technical progress, the technical documentation provides all the information necessary to assess the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in this Section"


§ `Regulative rules of Article 11`

DECLARE `Art 11(1) provider act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 11(1) use the simplified technical documentation form referred to in the paragraph`

-- src:314 | Where an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner, it shall use the form referred to in this paragraph.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, use of the form (src:314)
-- "it shall use": a duty of the SME or SMC with no time limit and no consequence stated, so no trace can show it breached (a late act reads FULFILLED). As amended only.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, and opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 11(1) provider act`
`Art 11(1) the SME's or SMC's duty to use the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted: the text has no such duty; nothing is owed
        WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
            IF `the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC, and opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner`
            THEN PARTY Provider
                 MUST `Art 11(1) use the simplified technical documentation form referred to in the paragraph`
                 HENCE FULFILLED
            ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the condition of the text is not met
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the Section does not apply on the date asked, or Article 2(2) cuts it off, or Article 2(13) says it may be limited

DECLARE `Art 11(1) notified body act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 11(1) accept the simplified technical documentation form for the purposes of the conformity assessment`

-- src:314 | Notified bodies shall accept the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, notified bodies accept the form (src:314)
-- "Notified bodies shall accept the form": no time limit and no consequence stated: no breach path. As amended only.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the documentation is provided on the form referred to in this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 11(1) notified body act`
`Art 11(1) the notified body's duty to accept the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted: the text has no such duty; nothing is owed
        WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
            IF `the documentation is provided on the form referred to in this paragraph`
            THEN PARTY `Notified body`
                 MUST `Art 11(1) accept the simplified technical documentation form for the purposes of the conformity assessment`
                 HENCE FULFILLED
            ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the condition of the text is not met
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the Section does not apply on the date asked, or Article 2(2) cuts it off, or Article 2(13) says it may be limited

DECLARE `Art 11(1) Commission act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 11(1) establish a simplified technical documentation form`

-- src:314 | To that end, the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782 | To that end, the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises.
@ref Art 11(1) second subparagraph, the Commission and the form (src:314) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:782)
-- "the Commission shall establish": a duty of the Commission with no time limit and no consequence stated: no breach path. In both versions; the Commission's duty is not tied to one AI system (fork F-commission-no-gate).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 2(13) body` `Art 11(1) Commission act`
